id: pm-5htunt
title: "Telemetry and Sentry scrubbers keep URL credentials whose host has no dot: attempted_args ships https://token@localhost and user:password@registry:8080 verbatim"
description: "Found 2026-11-10 while fixing pm-nhauur. Telemetry redaction of command arguments (sanitizeString/sanitizeCommandArgs in src/core/telemetry/runtime.ts) relies on redactEmailTokens, and Sentry's scrubString (src/core/sentry/instrument.ts) on an email regex that needs a dotted TLD. URL userinfo is only removed when it happens to look like an email address. Reproduced with the built CLI, an isolated PM_GLOBAL_PATH and PM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT pointed at an unreachable local port so events stay queued: 'pm package install https://tok3nSecret@localhost/x.tgz --bogus-flag' and 'pm package install https://u:p!ss-Secret9@registry:8080/x.tgz --bogus-flag' both queue a command_error event whose attempted_args contain the token and the password tail verbatim. A single-label host, a host:port, an IP literal or a password with a character outside the email local-part set defeats the heuristic. redactUrlsInText (GH-1660) only runs on error messages and only for scheme:// spellings. Fix: one conservative token rule shared with the CLI refusal path (pm-nhauur) — any token with a ':' before its last '@' has the span between them replaced — applied to every telemetry argument before the existing sanitizers and to every whitespace-delimited word of free text in both scrubbers. Duplicate check: searched 'telemetry url credentials attempted_args', 'GH-1660 redact urls telemetry'; pm-nhauur covers CLI stdout/stderr only."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: privacy,redaction,security,sentry,telemetry
created_at: "2026-11-10T12:54:03.603Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T14:35:42.216Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-10T14:35:38.558Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-10T14:35:38.558Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Telemetry attempted_args, attempted command and free-text fields remove the span between a token's first ':' and last '@' (keeping scheme slashes) before every other sanitizer, at both capture levels; Sentry scrubString applies the same rule to every whitespace-delimited word; Specs cover a single-label host, host:port, token-only userinfo, a password with characters outside the email local-part set, and a backslash authority; the existing diagnostic-privacy and telemetry redaction suites stay green"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "sanitizeCommandArgs applies redactUrlCredentialsInToken to each whole argument before sanitizeString. sanitizeCommonSensitiveTokens applies redactUrlCredentialsInText before the email heuristic at both capture levels, and Sentry scrubString applies the text rule before its other scrubbers."
expected_result: "No queued telemetry event or Sentry string carries URL userinfo for single-label hosts, host:port authorities, token-only userinfo, whitespace inside a password or backslash authorities."
actual_result: "A re-run of the queued-event reproduction against the new build (isolated global root, unreachable endpoint, Sentry disabled) shows zero secret bytes, with attempted_args showing https://[redacted]@... The telemetry-runtime and sentry-helpers specs pass with the new dotless-host, port, whitespace and backslash cases at both capture levels (121 tests in the linked command)."
